# Line endings, decided once, so nobody has to remember.
#
# WHY: 67 tracked files were CRLF and there was no .gitattributes, so the only protection was
# a human remembering to check `git diff --stat` per file — because a Python or byte-level
# write to a CRLF file rewrites EVERY line ending, and a one-line change then arrives as a
# whole-file diff that hides what actually changed. Several panel stylesheets are CRLF too.
#
# ADDING THIS LINE DID NOT CONVERT WHAT WAS ALREADY STORED (found by the T10 sweep, 2026-08-12,
# and fixed the same day). An attribute governs future checkouts; it does not touch the blobs
# already in the index. So for a week 44 tracked files still sat in git as CRLF while this file
# declared them LF — app/globals.css, lib/staffAuth.ts, lib/panelGate.ts, six
# components/Session*.tsx, app/login/*, three panel layouts, ~28 migrations, AGENTS.md, and
# docs/ACCESS-LADDER.md with MIXED endings. Each was one whole-file diff waiting to happen, and
# the "67" above had already drifted to 46, which means it had been happening quietly, one file
# at a time. `git add --renormalize` fixed the stored copies without touching a byte on disk.
#
# It cannot come back unnoticed: verify:ui (check 14, a PostToolUse hook + CI) fails when any
# tracked file is stored CRLF while its attribute says eol=lf. A file that is DELIBERATELY CRLF
# gets `-text` below, which is the honest way to say so.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.glb binary
*.gltf binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary

# The panel stylesheets and scripts are served as STATIC files and are currently CRLF.
# Left alone on purpose: normalising them would rewrite thousands of lines in files that are
# edited constantly, turning every future diff into noise for no benefit. New files get LF.
public/panels/**/*.css -text
public/panels/**/*.js  -text
